## Why This Is Asked

Balances privacy, regulatory needs, and system load by moving KYC attestation on-device.

### Key Concepts

- On-device cryptography and attestation
- Data minimization and privacy
- Key management and rotation
- Compliance and auditability

### Code Example

```javascript
async function signAttestation(privateKey, payload) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const data = enc.encode(JSON.stringify(payload));
  const sig = await crypto.subtle.sign({name: 'ECDSA', hash: 'SHA-256'}, privateKey, data);
  return btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(sig)));
}
```

### Follow-up Questions

- How to handle key compromise and revocation?
- What metrics drive break-even and rollout schedule?
- How to prevent replay attacks and ensure forward secrecy?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates understanding of edge cryptography implementation, privacy-preserving design, and business impact analysis in payment systems—skills critical for roles at Cloudflare, Square, and similar fintech companies.

## Key Concepts
- On-device cryptographic verification using Ed25519 and platform crypto APIs
- Key management lifecycle and rotation strategies
- Mobile device constraints: latency, CPU, memory, and energy budgets
- Local telemetry architecture and storage growth patterns
- Regulatory compliance frameworks for payment verification
- Financial modeling with go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify an Ed25519 signature on-device
async function verifyReceipt(receipt, publicKey) {
  // receipt: { data: ArrayBuffer, signature: ArrayBuffer }
  const isValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
    'Ed25519',
    publicKey,
    receipt.signature,
    receipt.data
  );
  return isValid;
}
```
